@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam ClassBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #ffffff

title What ChatHealthyLib gives every service, and what a concrete tool must supply in return

package "chathealthy_lib" {

  abstract class ChatHealthyTool {
    {static} TOOL_NAME : ClassVar[str]
    {static} TOOL_DESCRIPTION : ClassVar[str]
    {static} UTTERANCE_MANAGER_PROMPT : ClassVar[str]
    {static} .. exactly one of ..
    {static} NOT_UTTERANCE_ROUTABLE : marker
    {static} Request : ClassVar[Type[BaseModel]]
    {static} Response : ClassVar[Type[BaseModel]]
    --
    {abstract} + run(deps, request) : Response
    + run_and_log(deps, request) : Response
    - __init_subclass__()
  }

  class "tool Response" as ToolResponse <<BaseModel>> {
    + ... tool-specific answer fields ...
    + UserRefinementRequestText : str
  }

  class ChatHealthyException {
    + mode : str
    + message : str
    + server : str | None
    + component : str | None
    + exception : Exception | None
    + context : dict
    + construction_stack : str
  }

  class ChatHealthyLoggingService {
    + debug(msg, *args, exc, if_not_debug_log)
    + info(msg, *args, exc, if_not_debug_log)
    + warning(msg, *args, exc, if_not_debug_log)
    + error(msg, *args, exc, if_not_debug_log)
    + critical(msg, *args, exc, if_not_debug_log)
    + exception(msg, *args, exc, if_not_debug_log)
  }

  class ChatHealthyMongoUtilities {
    + getConnection(identity, cluster, host="") : TimedClient
  }

  class "merge_returning_document()" as Merge <<lib function>> {
    serial and deterministic
    the sole merge site
  }

  class AgentDeps <<dataclass>> {
    + user_object : UserObject
    + session_token : SessionToken
    + mongo_frontend
    + server_env : str
    + stream : StreamSink
  }

  class "extract_location()" as Geo <<lib function>> {
    single-purpose model call
    mines a geography from an utterance
    resolves free-text geo incl. misspellings
  }
}

class "ToolRegistry" as Registry <<Mongo doc>> {
  ChatHealthyToolRegistrySchema
  --
  tools + routes + pages
  a page carries members,
  required_members, completeness
  instance{build, commit, env, live}
  --
  one document per build per env
  one live instance per env
  presence IS the allowlist
  subscriptions ARE the dispatch table
  may_call IS the call map
}

package "SharedServices" {
  class UniversalNavigator {
    TOOL_NAME = "universal_navigator"
    NOT_UTTERANCE_ROUTABLE
    --
    + run(deps, request)
    .. the main; holds no data ..
  }

  class UtteranceManager {
    TOOL_NAME = "utterance_manager"
    UTTERANCE_MANAGER_PROMPT = preamble
    --
    + run(deps, utterance) : dispatch set
    .. RequestUsersRefinement (capability) ..
    + RequestUsersRefinement()
    + RequestUsersRefinement(question : string)
  }
}

package "satellite server" {
  class UniversalNavigatorProxy {
    + relay(tool_name, request)
    + apply_metadata_change(slice)
    .. tool-to-tool traffic only ..
  }
}

Exception <|-- ChatHealthyException
ChatHealthyTool <|-- UniversalNavigator
ChatHealthyTool <|-- UtteranceManager

ChatHealthyTool ..> AgentDeps : run(deps, ...)
ChatHealthyTool ..> ToolResponse : run returns
ChatHealthyTool ..> ChatHealthyException : raises when a subclass\nomits a class attribute
ChatHealthyLoggingService ..> ChatHealthyException : exc= must be one
UniversalNavigator ..> Merge : merges every\nreturning document
UniversalNavigator ..> Registry : reads the live\ndoc at startup
UniversalNavigator ..> UniversalNavigatorProxy : hands the metadata slice;\ninternal callbacks return here
UtteranceManager ..> Registry : preamble + every fragment\nassemble the routing table

note right of ChatHealthyTool #f3f4f6
  A subclass supplies its class attributes and one run
  method. __init_subclass__ refuses the class at import
  if any is missing, so a tool cannot be half declared
  and discovered at dispatch time. Exactly one of
  UTTERANCE_MANAGER_PROMPT or NOT_UTTERANCE_ROUTABLE is
  required -- silence refuses the build. The build-time
  generator reads TOOL_DESCRIPTION and that choice from
  source by AST into the one registry document.

  run_and_log records the invocation whether run
  returned or raised.
end note

note bottom of ToolResponse #f3f4f6
  Every tool Response carries UserRefinementRequestText.
  Populated => the tool is ASKING the user a question, which
  the UtteranceManager delivers via
  RequestUsersRefinement(question). Empty => the tool is
  answering.
end note

note bottom of ChatHealthyMongoUtilities #f3f4f6
  No connection string and no password. The certificate is
  the credential: identity selects the X.509 cert and
  therefore the MongoDB user and its grants. There is
  deliberately no fallback, because a fallback to a shared
  credential makes the whole model decorative.
end note

note bottom of ChatHealthyException #f3f4f6
  Catch sites discriminate on mode, never on type.
  External exceptions keep their native type until a
  boundary converts them, and the conversion carries the
  original in exception= so the mode says what kind of
  failure it was and the original says what failed.
end note

note right of UniversalNavigator #f3f4f6
  The main, and the only node that accepts external
  traffic. Reads the registry map and drives the route;
  tests parameter completeness (a conflict is an
  exception); owns the render ledger (dispatch records the
  expectation, the completion callback closes it, the
  timeout facts race it); merges returning documents
  serially via the lib; manages sessions and external
  calls; hands the proxies their metadata and propagates
  runtime changes; instruments every failure.
end note

note bottom of UtteranceManager #f3f4f6
  Non-blocking: sees an utterance, decides whether it is
  sufficient to dispatch to one or more tools, and dispatches
  if so. That decision IS its job. The old classifier is gone
  -- preamble plus every tool's fragment in, routes out, the
  agent dispatches.

  RequestUsersRefinement is a capability of this manager, not
  a tool the navigator dispatches, so a tool never speaks to
  the user directly. Two forms, both here: RequestUsersRefinement()
  where this manager's own LLM authors the question when
  classification finds no dispatchable route or a missing slot,
  and RequestUsersRefinement(question) where a dispatched tool
  authored the question and this manager delivers it.
end note

note bottom of Geo #f3f4f6
  OPEN ARCHITECTURAL QUESTION (unresolved): does location
  extraction stay in the shared library every front-end
  component installs? It is a live single-purpose model
  call and fails test 2 of the boundary rule; it is the
  template for four other single-purpose model-call modules
  in the same position. Either move it out to a page-scoped
  Geo tool (individualProvider + facility, parallel to the
  specialty/NUCC filter), or grant the boundary a stated
  exception.
end note

note bottom of UniversalNavigatorProxy #f3f4f6
  One per satellite server. Relays tool-to-tool traffic
  both ways -- local is a function call, remote crosses the
  wire to the main. Holds the metadata slice the main gave
  it; refuses work on stale metadata. No sessions, no
  ledger, no merge, no external calls. Instruments every
  failed relay.
end note

@enduml
